<h2>eu-inc Weekly | 2026-W10</h2>
<p>A quiet week for EU-Inc with no major legislative developments, though the proposal continues to generate discussion around tax competition implications for smaller member states.</p>
<h3>This Week</h3>
<p><strong><a href="https://es.euronews.com/my-europe/2026/02/03/que-es-eu-inc-cual-es-su-plan-para-que-las-empresas-europeas-operen-sin-fronteras">¿Qué es EU-INC y cuál es su plan para que las empresas europeas operen sin fronteras?</a></strong> (Euronews ES)
Euronews Spanish-language explainer covering von der Leyen's EU-INC announcement and the digital incorporation framework.</p>
<p><strong><a href="https://x.com/kolokasi_sotira/status/2030053429830148194">@kolokasi_sotira on X</a></strong> (X/Twitter)
Commentary framing the 28th jurisdiction as eroding the "low taxes moat" that smaller member states rely on to attract companies.</p>
<h3>New Arguments</h3>
<ul>
<li>❌ The 28th jurisdiction removes the competitive advantage of low-tax member states, undermining their economic model (@kolokasi_sotira)</li>
</ul>
<h3>Radar</h3>
<ul>
<li>🌍 Cyprus-linked account engaging with EU-Inc debate, raising small-state tax competition concerns</li>
</ul>]]></description>
